DATASUM = '0       '           / data unit checksum updated 2026-08-13T13:34:28 COMMENT Reference file created by refstis.functions                             HISTORY Superdark image, combination of 3.0 input dark frames taken in          HISTORY CCDGAIN=-1, BINAXIS1=1, BINAXIS2=1 mode.                                HISTORY All input frames were from Proposal(s) 12345:                           HISTORY title                                                                   HISTORY The following input files were used:                                    HISTORY testdark1_raw.fits                                                      HISTORY testdark2_raw.fits                                                      HISTORY testdark3_raw.fits                                                      HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY This superdark image is a combination of 2 images.                      HISTORY The first is a "baseline dark" image which is a                         HISTORY (typically) monthly average of (cosmic-ray-rejected)                    HISTORY dark files. The second image is made locally within the                 HISTORY "weekdark" script.                                                      HISTORY These gain -1 darks are first                                           HISTORY corrected for temperature (C) using the factor                          HISTORY 1.0 / (1.0 + DRK_V_TMP * (OCCDHTAV - S2_REF_TEMP)) and then             HISTORY combined together (cosmic rays are rejected in the                      HISTORY combination) using calstis,                                             HISTORY and normalized to a dark time of 1 second. After that,                  HISTORY hot pixels in that normalized dark are updated into the                 HISTORY baseline dark. These hot pixels have a value higher than                HISTORY (baseline dark current + 5 sigma of the new dark).                      HISTORY The pixels hotter than 0.1 electron/sec in this dark                    HISTORY are being assigned a DQ value of 16.                                    HISTORY Previously hot pixels that have fully annealed out                      HISTORY between the observing dates of the baseline and the                     HISTORY new dark are being assigned a value equal to that in                    HISTORY a median-filtered (kernel = 5x5 pixels) version of                      HISTORY the baseline dark.                                                      END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     